rcia-became-one-of-the-worlds-most-strategic-military-bases-after-its-entire-population-was-removed-from-the-island/articleshow/132604273.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-24T23:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132604273,imgsize-2156978.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Retired police officer discovers an exceptionally rare white rattlesnake in Arizona, “once-in-a-lifetime” find]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132606883.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/retired-police-officer-discovers-an-exceptionally-rare-white-rattlesnake-in-arizona-once-in-a-lifetime-find/articleshow/132606883.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/retired-police-officer-discovers-an-exceptionally-rare-white-rattlesnake-in-arizona-once-in-a-lifetime-find/articleshow/132606883.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-24T18:50:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132606980,imgsize-1522501.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1,600-year-old Roman guardian spirit found beneath ancient fort in northern England]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132607177.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[At Vindolanda fort, archaeologists have made an exciting discovery: a sandstone carving of a Roman guardian spirit, estimated to be 1,600 years old. This striking relief depicts a genius, symbolising the protective spirit revered by the soldiers. Such archaeological finds deepen our understanding of the spiritual lives and beliefs of Roman forces stationed at this military stronghold, adding to the fort's historical narrative.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/1600-year-old-roman-guardian-spirit-discovered-beneath-ancient-fort-in-northern-england-reveals-how-soldiers-sought-divine-protection/articleshow/132607177.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/1600-year-old-roman-guardian-spirit-discovered-beneath-ancient-fort-in-northern-england-reveals-how-soldiers-sought-divine-protection/articleshow/132607177.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-24T19:15:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132607241,imgsize-1325666.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Seattle's 'Emerald City' from space: How glaciers and people shaped its landscape]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132607410.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ancient glaciers sculpted Seattle's hills and valleys thousands of years ago. Humans later reshaped this terrain through extensive engineering projects. The city's development is closely tied to its numerous waterways and coastlines. These natural and man-made features create the distinctive "Emerald City" landscape. Nasa's image reveals this combined geological and engineering history.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/seattles-emerald-city-from-space-how-glaciers-and-people-shaped-its-landscape/articleshow/132607410.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/seattles-emerald-city-from-space-how-glaciers-and-people-shaped-its-landscape/articleshow/132607410.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-24T19:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132607481,imgsize-1517114.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists discover a 17-million-year-old ape fossil in Egypt that could rewrite early ape evolution]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132609819.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A new fossil ape named Masripithecus was found in northern Egypt. This discovery suggests northeastern Africa played a larger role in early ape evolution. Previously, East Africa was considered the primary region for ape diversification. The Masripithecus fossil fills a geographical and evolutionary gap in scientific understanding. This find expands the map of early hominoid origins beyond East Africa.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/scientists-discover-a-17-million-year-old-ape-fossil-in-egypt-that-could-rewrite-early-ape-evolution/articleshow/132609819.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/scientists-discover-a-17-million-year-old-ape-fossil-in-egypt-that-could-rewrite-early-ape-evolution/articleshow/132609819.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-24T21:34:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132609912,imgsize-155417.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[8 people entered a sealed glass world believing they could survive for two years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132605750.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/8-people-entered-a-sealed-glass-world-believing-they-could-survive-for-two-years-then-the-oxygen-began-to-disappear/articleshow/132605750.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/8-people-entered-a-sealed-glass-world-believing-they-could-survive-for-two-years-then-the-oxygen-began-to-disappear/articleshow/132605750.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-24T22:18:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132605750,imgsize-2595459.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Prince William’s Duchy of Cornwall is helping double one of the last surviving temperate rainforests]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132609140.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/prince-williams-duchy-of-cornwall-is-helping-double-one-of-englands-last-surviving-temperate-rainforests-where-1250-young-trees-have-already-been-planted/articleshow/132609140.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/prince-williams-duchy-of-cornwall-is-helping-double-one-of-englands-last-surviving-temperate-rainforests-where-1250-young-trees-have-already-been-planted/articleshow/132609140.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-24T22:08:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132610398,imgsize-394016.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian man dies in road accident in Detroit; his two-wheeler was hit by a car; developed cerebral fat embolism]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132609690.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-man-dies-in-road-accident-in-detroit-his-two-wheeler-was-hit-by-a-car-developed-cerebral-fat-embolism/articleshow/132609690.c